ent with a margin near twelve points.", "watch": "A late influx of outside spending against Harrigan or a major scandal could narrow the race, but no such evidence has emerged.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Pat Harrigan (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Pat Harrigan seeks a term representing this R+9 North Carolina district against Democrat Ashley Bell and Libertarian Steve Feldman. Harrigan has out-raised Bell roughly nine to one and holds about $463,000 on hand, while Bell's campaign has minimal cash and no outside support on either side. Every major race rater places the district in the Republican column, most calling it Solid or Safe R.\n\nThe only available poll, a Republican-sponsored March survey of likely voters, gave Harrigan a 13- to 14-point lead. Prediction markets price his win probability around 95%. Harrigan has spent the fall publicizing bipartisan legislation on AI, veterans' issues, and fraud enforcement. The forecast expects Harrigan to win by roughly twelve points, with Bell needing an extraordinary shift to make the race competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0414, "margin": -11.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0292, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0146, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0158, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0277, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0297, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0233, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0